    {
      "id": 143564,
      "name": "The Burning Stickman",
      "username": "The_Burning_Stickman",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_burning_stickman/{size}/2003_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-06-30T22:03:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Man, I really wish we'd realized that a couple weeks ago (because of a really bad opening draw -- Profane Summons, which drew not only Orb of Delirium, but also Tome of the Unknowable and Ruins of Malediction -- he had almost his entire deck out on the playing field by the end of the second round and was one of only two games we've played where we got to the point of needing a villain deck reshuffle). Admittedly Ruins of Malediction's DR made it so that most of the mass damage attacks couldn't do much anyway, but still, we misinterpreted it as more like Legacy's Heroic Interception and focused mainly on attacks that would damage the Orb directly.</p><p>That was actually a really fun game -- we played mostly the mystic heroes (Nightmist, Ra, Fanatic, Argent Adept and Tempest), which meant when Apostate played Apocalypse, it did him more harm than us by wiping out his demons and leaving Nightmist, Ra, and Fanatic's relics on the table.</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:21:00.873Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
