      "username": "The_Burning_Stickman",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_burning_stickman/{size}/2003_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-07-01T14:15:53.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ameena\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/48/1907_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ameena:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Just to check something…you know you never  have  to draw during your draw phase, right? You only ever  have  to if something says \"draw a card\" (as opposed to \"you  may  draw a card\"). So you can avoid Apostate playing extra cards via the Tome at the cost of not getting any extra cards yourself.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yeah, we know, but it came out on the first round. Nightmist and Argent Adept both <em>need</em> card draw to even basically function, and nobody else had any powers in their flops that could get through the +2 damage reduction from the Runes to even start on the Orb. If we didn't draw, we couldn't do much but plink at Apostate himself, so we judged it worth letting him put more stuff out so we could actually get moving.</p>",
